{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>One who strikes a man and he dies.</b> Rashi explained that the verse here is ״מכה איש״ and the verse ״איש כי יכה״ and the verse nearby ״וכי יזיד״ — it was not necessary to write ״מכה״ at all. However, one may say that if only these two verses were written, one would have said specifically a man [ish] who killed, but not a woman, and not a tumtum, and not an androginus. And thus Rashi explained regarding ״וגונב איש״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:39.056339320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}